                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0ed0f030-4920-302b-941b-4641cea2c3c0",
                        "entry_id": "6c20975f-3311-3b87-b539-a607935e3d6e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To reverse the direction of (a current)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "59c317c7-7ac6-4484-903c-3d862c3b1709",
                                "sense_id": "0ed0f030-4920-302b-941b-4641cea2c3c0",
                                "text": "Continuously rated machines shall be required to commutate successfully momentary loads of 150% of the Amperes corresponding to the continuous rating keeping the rheostat set for rated load excitation."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ea932cc-110b-31f8-b5f0-cde49bed67cc",
                        "entry_id": "6c20975f-3311-3b87-b539-a607935e3d6e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To convert from being or using an alternating current into being or using a direct current."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d5e4f2f-0a35-47a0-86e7-a86840d6c537",
                                "sense_id": "3ea932cc-110b-31f8-b5f0-cde49bed67cc",
                                "text": "In line commutation, advantage of the a.c. supply going through zero value at every half-cycle is taken to commutate the thyristor."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "dffd8f0d-0885-3c82-aede-aa783a562358",
                        "entry_id": "6c20975f-3311-3b87-b539-a607935e3d6e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To commute; to be invariant under a reversal of the positions of operands."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "61929744-fc56-4b0e-8bae-c04fd36adeed",
                                "sense_id": "dffd8f0d-0885-3c82-aede-aa783a562358",
                                "text": "The match of two finite line segments in 2 dimensions requires 2 translations, 1 rotation, 1 scale transformation; the order is here important, and these operators cannot commutate."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e784ce10-07dc-3c2d-a2ce-7db8e3b8129b",
                        "entry_id": "6c20975f-3311-3b87-b539-a607935e3d6e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To commute; to change one kind of payment into another, especially to convert from several installments to a single lumpsum payment."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5d5a56f5-7ba2-44dc-8533-e7e004bbfb52",
                                "sense_id": "e784ce10-07dc-3c2d-a2ce-7db8e3b8129b",
                                "text": "Ah, commutation. I knew there was something else. This is where you can commutate your weekly payments into a lump sum and be rid of the “system”."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4d7f4f75-9a87-3dbf-9dc6-3921f0fcd3fa",
                        "entry_id": "6c20975f-3311-3b87-b539-a607935e3d6e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To remove or reduce the legal obligations or restrictions on"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "89363ed1-4f38-43c7-9d56-a2688dbe1461",
                                "sense_id": "4d7f4f75-9a87-3dbf-9dc6-3921f0fcd3fa",
                                "text": "Specifically, the seminary was challenged by industrial millers who petitioned to build steam-powered mills and by large Montreal property holders who demanded that the crown commutate their lands."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b9ee67b6-2196-38e4-90df-eaeabef3a9fa",
                        "entry_id": "6c20975f-3311-3b87-b539-a607935e3d6e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To transform, especially into a reversed or opposite form."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "76f3f32d-c469-433e-aefb-4e3798e77f10",
                                "sense_id": "b9ee67b6-2196-38e4-90df-eaeabef3a9fa",
                                "text": "Writers change the URIs as they compose because writers commutate and manipulate language to create a variety of rhetorical experiences that can be read at once, as overlapping, or as separate."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
